module product.p4261.e1_body_sightings

// THE BODIES THAT WERE SEEN AND NEVER READ. One row per E1 position where an atlas frame
// shows a part fitted and no marking was read: the designator as printed, the frame by its SHA-256,
// and the region the sighting record boxed. product.p4261.e1_b turns these into
// InstalledComponent rows whose identification is BodySeenMarkingUnread -- presence from a photo, with no
// claim about what the part is. The atlas's kind word is not carried: a kind is not an
// identification and no consumer reads it yet (DESIGN §3c).
//
// Generated by gen_e1_body_sightings_dag.py (private branch p4261/e1-atlas-handoff, commit 2d9f1424c21226f189cdf9fc605d59e4607e7b7a)
// from per_photo_readings.jsonl and per_photo_readings_sd_2026-11-03.jsonl and per_photo_readings_sd_2026-11-06.jsonl beside it, over the positions the
// e1_position_receipts generator admitted, skipping every position e1_b
// records a body or a held row for. THE RULE, clause by clause, with how a reader audits each.
// The clauses the model can see are checked by a named test; the two that live only in the
// receipts name the field to read there. No clause is left to trust the script for.
//   admitted    the designator is admitted as a position by the position-receipts generator:
//               read certain and complete, above the passive level, with no '*' or '?'.
//               Audited by every_body_sighting_is_at_a_position_the_authority_admitted.
//   needs a row it carries neither an InstalledComponent nor an UnresolvedPart in
//               e1_b. A second row about one footprint would read as a second
//               observation of the same instance. Audited by
//               no_body_row_is_a_second_claim_about_an_instance.
//   sighted     a per-photo sighting for that exact designator records a body of a kind the
//               generator enumerates (BODY_KINDS) at standing "confirmed". Tentative is not
//               enough to say a body is fitted, so a position resting on one is refused here and
//               belongs among the held rows instead. Audited from the receipts' kind and standing
//               fields, which are the referent and are not copied into the model.
//   resolvable  the digest the sighting record carries is a row of the photograph store. A frame
//               outside the store gets a typed gap in the photograph layer, never a digest
//               invented to look like one (DESIGN §5), so this generator refuses rather than
//               emit it. Audited by the_real_e1_judges_every_image_reading, whose pinned counts go
//               red if a row points at a frame the store lacks; the control that proves the test
//               bites is a_citation_to_bytes_the_store_does_not_hold_is_refused.
//   held        the designators named below, refused because the frames disagree about the same
//               footprint. Audited by what_the_body_rule_refused_is_held_with_the_frames_to_compare.
// One row per position, grain A: among its qualifying sightings a boxed one is kept ahead of an
// unboxed one, and among equals the lower photo id, because a region a reader can open is worth
// more than one they cannot. The other sightings stay in the receipts, not in the model.
//
// 66 rows: 42 carry the sighting record's own pixel box; 24 leave
// the region Absent, because the 2026-11-02 pass recorded where the body was as prose with a point
// and not a box, and a width and a height invented here would be a fabricated measurement in the
// one place the model is meant to be checkable against an image.
//
// REFUSED BY RULE, whether or not they appear below: D1_P1 (one frame sights a diode body, another sights the same footprint empty); U3_P3 (one frame sights an IC body, another sights the nearest IC outline empty); U40 (its only sighting gives kind 'unknown', which does not say a body is fitted).
// Those three are recorded on the board as UnresolvedPart with an obligation naming the frames, not
// dropped: the atlas looked, and what it saw is not enough to write either fitted or empty.
// REFUSED ON THE DATA, 0 of them this time
// (a position already carrying a body or a held row on the board is skipped before the data is
// consulted, so the three above do not appear here once their held rows exist).

import std.content_hash { Sha256Digest, Sha256DigestHex }
import std.nat { Nat }
import std.optional { Absent, Present }
import std.types { List, NonEmptyStr }
import product.electrical.photograph { PixelRegion }

// One body sighted in one frame. `designator` is the string on the silkscreen, carried verbatim;
// `content` is the frame's SHA-256 and must name a row of product.p4261.e1_photographs, which is
// where its Drive folder and file name live -- they are not repeated here, because a name is
// carried in one place or it drifts (DESIGN §3), and nothing in the model reads it (DESIGN §3c);
// `region` is where in that frame the sighting record pointed, when it pointed with a box. The
// frame's name in the comment above each row is provenance for a reader comparing this file with
// the per-photo receipts, not a field of the model.
type BodySighting {
  designator: NonEmptyStr
  content: Sha256DigestHex
  region: PixelRegion?
}

